## Three layers (do not collapse)

| Layer | Field | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| **Featured** | `featuredWindows` | Home carousel — **temporary** (~2–3 weeks per pick) |
| **Collection** | `collectionEventIds` | Full “See all” close-to-home set — **season-long** while valid |
| **Drive** | `driveEventIds` | “Worth a little drive” — **stable** anchors; rotate less often |

## Featured rotation

- Default featured duration: **~2–3 weeks** per pick.
- Rotate **at least 1–2 cards every ~2 weeks** so the carousel stays fresh.
- Keep **3–6 cards** active on any given day (overlap windows briefly during handoffs).
- Mark **1–2 anchor slots** (`anchor: true`) — festival weekends, strong seasonal rows.
- Use `note` on each window for launch-review context.
- Resolve Home carousel with `resolveFeaturedSeasonalEvents()` / `getFeaturedEventIdsForDate()` — **never** a static ID list.

## Theme transitions

- **One seasonal theme module at a time** — `activeFrom` / `activeUntil` do not overlap.
- **Transition week:** blend **1–2 picks from the next theme** into the current theme’s `featuredWindows` before the module title swaps.
- Preview picks live on the **outgoing** theme until the swap; then move primary home to the **incoming** theme.

## Drive picks

- Special outings **outside core cities** — not every farm needs a drive slot.
- Prefer **1–2 stable drive anchors** per theme.
- Do not duplicate next-theme drive picks in the current collection long-term — preview in transition only.

## Adding a new seasonal pick (checklist)

1. Pass the **universal litmus test** for this theme.
2. Ensure the event exists in catalog (sheet, staging, or `seasonal*DriveEvents.ts`).
3. Add to **`collectionEventIds`** (close to home) or **`driveEventIds`** (worth a drive) — not both unless intentional.
4. Add **`featuredWindows`** only when spotlighting on Home for a specific period.
5. Update **`SEASONAL_THEME_SCHEDULE`** if theme dates or transition notes change.
6. Verify on `/experiment/seasonal-launch-review`; confirm badges stay off on seasonal surfaces.

